---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { LEGAL_HOLDER } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="The Bead Reserve : Accessibility"
  description="The accessibility statement for The Bead Reserve's website, with its conformance status and how to report a barrier."
>
  <main>
    <article class="policy bracket-frame">
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This is an accessibility statement from {LEGAL_HOLDER} for The Bead
          Reserve website.
        </p>

        <h2>Conformance status</h2>
        <p>
          The
          <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/"
            >Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)</a
          >
          define requirements for designers and developers to improve
          accessibility for people with disabilities. They define three levels
          of conformance: Level A, Level AA, and Level AAA. The Bead Reserve is
          partially conformant with WCAG 2.2 Level AA. Partially conformant
          means that some parts of the content do not fully conform to the
          accessibility standard.
        </p>

        <h2>Feedback</h2>
        <p>
          If you encounter an accessibility barrier on this site, please let me
          know:
        </p>
        <PolicyContact />
        <p>I try to respond to feedback as quickly as possible.</p>

        <h2>Technical specifications</h2>
        <p>
          Accessibility of this site relies on the following technologies
          working with your browser and any assistive technologies or plugins
          installed on your computer:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>HTML</li>
          <li>CSS</li>
          <li>JavaScript</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Limitations and alternatives</h2>
        <p>
          Despite my best efforts, there may be limitations. Known limitations:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            The reserve monitor is a black screen in both themes on purpose. Its
            state is also given in text, in the badge and the captions. The
            camera frame has alt text.
          </li>
          <li>
            The reserve seal turns over on hover or keyboard focus. Its label
            states the reserve figure and names the reverse. The genesis count
            it carries also appears in the reserve figures.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>Please contact me if you observe an issue not listed above.</p>

        <h2>Assessment approach</h2>
        <p>
          Curt Henrichs assessed the accessibility of this site by
          self-evaluation. Every change to the site also runs an automated WCAG
          2.2 A and AA check (axe-core) against every page, in both the light
          and dark themes, including the reserve monitor opened full size, plus
          a keyboard walk of the home page's focus order and an HTML validation
          of every built page.
        </p>

        <h2>Date</h2>
        <p>
          This statement was created on 7 October 2026 and revised on 8 October
          2026.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
